# Generated at build time by scripts/buildInstaller.cjs and packaged into the app
# so it can report its own build-time limits at runtime. Machine-specific: it
# records the readiness verdict of whichever machine produced the build, so
# committing it would ship one machine's verdict as if it described every build.
# electron-builder packages from the working tree, not from git, so ignoring it
# here does not stop it shipping.
shared/buildManifest.json

# Agent and workflow scratch. `.agents/` holds per-run plans, review verdicts and
# task metadata; `.worktrees/` holds git worktrees for in-flight workflow runs.
# Both are working state, not source: a worktree is a second checkout of this very
# repository, so a `git add .` with these untracked would commit a whole duplicate
# tree. Research documents that the spec CITES are committed under docs/research/
# instead — the copies that appear under .agents/ are duplicates of those, so
# ignoring this directory loses no cited source.
.agents/
.worktrees/

# Runtime data — encrypted stores, salt, verifier, scenario memory, logs.
# Never committed: rama.salt and rama.verify are per-machine, and the .enc
# domains are the user's data. Committing them would also let an attacker
# attempt an offline attack against the passcode.
data/
*.enc
rama.salt
rama.verify
.nucleus.enc
.nucleus.salt
